From: Felix Fietkau <nbd@nbd.name>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 07:42:25 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] AP MLD: Remove a link only when it is on the list

hostapd_bss_link_deinit() takes hapd->started to mean that the BSS is
linked to its AP MLD, but hostapd_setup_bss() sets hapd->started before
the link joins the AP MLD. A setup that fails in between, for example in
hostapd_drv_link_add(), reaches hostapd_mld_remove_link() with a list
node that was never added, and dl_list_del() dereferences NULL. The
failure paths of hostapd_add_iface() and
hostapd_setup_interface_complete_sync() take this path.

dl_list_del() clears the node and a BSS is allocated zeroed, so
hapd->link.next is NULL exactly when the node is on no list. Skip the
removal in that case.

Signed-off-by: Felix Fietkau <nbd@nbd.name>
---

--- a/src/ap/hostapd.c
+++ b/src/ap/hostapd.c
@@ -5572,6 +5572,11 @@ int hostapd_mld_remove_link(struct hosta
 	if (!mld)
 		return -1;
 
+	/* hostapd_setup_bss() sets hapd->started before the link joins the
+	 * MLD, so a setup that failed in between reaches here unlinked. */
+	if (!hapd->link.next)
+		return 0;
+
 	dl_list_del(&hapd->link);
 	mld->num_links--;
 
